    "updated_at": "2018-02-05T21:52:11Z",
    "body": "Right, any issues filed on the spec are about what the spec supports, I'd assume. So I'm not sure why that's an argument against #1246.\r\n\r\nHow a browser chooses to implement the spec's requirements is up to the browser. Sometimes they do so by typing C++ to implement the spec directly, or sometimes they do so by using code generation techniques (either Web IDL driven, or otherwise). But that doesn't change how the spec normatively defines features.\r\n\r\nIn this case, what interface an element implements is normatively defined by https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#elements-in-the-dom:element-interface. Browsers can feel free to implement that algorithm using Web IDL if they want, but I don't think Web IDL is a good tool for expressing that algorithm.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
